Xray-core: dial a sinkhole address by its sniffed name

Iran's filter answers a blocked name with an address in 10.10.34.0/24. An
application that looked the name up before the tunnel came up still holds
that answer. With routeOnly sniffing the core used the sniffed name only to
route and still dialled the address, so the connection went out directly to
the sinkhole (the range is private) and failed. On 2026-10-02 apps on 59 of
161 phones did this while connected: Instagram, WhatsApp, Facebook.

For a connection headed to a sinkhole address the sniffed name replaces the
address, as it would without routeOnly. Nothing legitimate lives in that
range, so no other connection changes, and routeOnly keeps its reason
everywhere else: a Telegram fake-TLS proxy presents a name that is not its
own.

Base:    github.com/xtls/xray-core v1.260327.1-0.20260728075948-5ca6f4b7d4dc
         (v26.7.28), applied after xray-autoselect.patch.
Licence: MPL-2.0, the same as Xray-core.

